---
// Unlisted. For the organization only. Not linked from the site.
import '../../styles/fraunces.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';
import { BERLIN_DESK } from '../../data/berlin';

const q = `desk=${BERLIN_DESK}&dl=1`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Berlin desk · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p class="kicker">AUTOMA Chem · Estrel Berlin · 26 October · 9:40</p>
      <h1>For the organization</h1>
      <p class="deck">The film and the roadmap. Not on the public site until after the talk.</p>
      <p class="files">
        <a href={`/api/berlin/roadmap.pdf?${q}`}>Download the roadmap</a>
        <a href={`/api/berlin/film.mp4?${q}`}>Download the film</a>
      </p>

      <section class="means" aria-label="What the animation means">
        <p class="kicker">What the animation means</p>
        <h2>One sheet. Two distances.</h2>
        <p>
          The film is not a decoration in front of the talk. It is the talk, drawn.
          One sheet of paper starts as a plan and has to survive the walk.
        </p>
        <p>
          It opens with an architect drawing from above. The drawing becomes Brasília:
          precise from the air, and a long way from the person on the ground.
          That is the argument. Governance designed from the helicopter does not
          always work for the person who has to live with it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then the sheet has to carry a number. It looks like chemistry. On the paper
          it is a data product: a road, a source, and someone who can stand behind it.
          You cannot report what you cannot trace.
        </p>
        <p>
          The lines speed up. AI does not invent a clearer meaning. It scales the one
          that is already there. A digital twin is only useful when an operator trusts
          it and a person is accountable when it is wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          The sheet ends where a person is still in the drawing. Agents do not own risk.
          Humans do.
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><span>00</span> Two distances. The title, before the drawing starts.</li>
          <li><span>01</span> The architect. A plan, made from above.</li>
          <li><span>02</span> Brasília. Perfect in plan. Different on the ground.</li>
          <li><span>03</span> The number. Ambition has to become evidence.</li>
          <li><span>04</span> AI scales what is already there.</li>
          <li><span>05</span> The twin. A drawing someone has to trust.</li>
          <li><span>06</span> The close. Humans do. Always.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html, body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100svh;
    background: var(--void);
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  main {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 14vh 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .kicker {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 0.95;
  }

  .deck {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--flesh);
  }

  .files {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
  }

  a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bronze);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.7);
  }

  a:hover { color: var(--gold); }

  .means { margin-top: 4.5rem; padding-top: 1.6rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.45); }

  h2 {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .means p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--flesh);
  }

  ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.14);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  li span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }
</style>
